MpVFX is "open core": the app in this repository is open source; the two engines it runs on are not.

1. The app: everything in this repository (the Swift editor in mpvfx-swift/, its tests, documentation, installers,
   scripts and CI) is licensed under either of

     * the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE, or http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0), or
     * the MIT license (LICENSE-MIT, or http://opensource.org/licenses/MIT),

   at your option. SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0. Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any
   contribution intentionally submitted for inclusion in it by you, as defined in the Apache-2.0 license, shall be
   dual licensed as above, without any additional terms or conditions.

2. The engines are proprietary and are NOT covered by the licences above: the media engine (library mpvfx_ffi) and
   the keyframe engine (library cvkf). Their source code is not in this repository. The app downloads them as
   prebuilt binaries (the versions and SHA-256 checksums in mpvfx-swift/binaries.lock) from the public releases of
   https://github.com/marshiyar/mpvfx-media-binaries, and the installers ship them next to the app. Each binary
   release carries its own licence, which governs its use and redistribution; being able to download a binary
   grants no other right. Their C headers are distributed with the binaries under the same terms, and each binary's
   NOTICE lists the third-party code inside it; the installers include both files.

   The app's own Swift adapters over those headers (mpvfx-swift/Sources/OneTakeMedia and OneTakeKeyframes) are part
   of the app and licensed as in 1.
